{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1481601-good-manga-inspirations-for-changeling-the-lost","id":1481601,"title":"Good Manga inspirations for Changeling The Lost?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-21T09:05:04-07:00","id":1481601,"title":"Good Manga inspirations for Changeling The Lost?","content":"Do you have some Manga books that you just think just suits the game perfectly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T16:11:29-07:00","id":1481624,"title":"","content":"I use various things from my favorite manga books for <i>Changeling</i> inspirations, even if some of the works I use for inspirations aren't in the same genre.<br /> <br /> <i>Nurarihyon no Mago, Dororo</i>, and other manga featuring youkai often serve as inspirations, since I often use youkai as inspiration for changelings, hobgoblins, Huntsmen, and True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:26:31-07:00","id":1481796,"title":"","content":"<i>King Of Thorn </i>is a very good one too, it has a very Changeling premise and twist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T19:56:34-07:00","id":1481808,"title":"","content":"I would recommend Rumiko Takahashi most recent work, <b><i>Mao, </i></b>which is about a girl who gets cursed by a cat spirit and gains some of it's powers. It is similiar to her earlier work, Inuyasha, in that she finds a barrier that allows her to travel through time (to the 1920's).<br /> <br /> I would also recommend <b><i>Kemono Jihen, </i></b>which is about a Japanese boy who is half-ghoul (A western type Youkai) and half-human. He joins a detective agency whose official duties it solve occult issues, but real project is to bring an understanding between humans and Youkai. The series has not been translated into English, but you can find it here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.mangahere.cc/manga/kemono_jihen/\" target=\"_blank\">Kemono Jihen Manga - Read Kemono Jihen Online at MangaHere</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T20:09:06-07:00","id":1481810,"title":"","content":"Another manga series I am enjoying and I feel can be a HUGE source of inspiration for a changeling game is <b><i>Mahou Tsukai no Yome/The Ancient Magus Bride.</i></b> The premise of the series is that a Japanese girl, Chise Hatori, is sold at an auction due to being a Sleigh Beggy, a special type of mage who can draw on power from her surroundings and within herself. She is bought by a fae being, Elias Ainsworth, to be his wife. The series fits the <b><i>Changeling: The Lost</i></b> theme of trauma as it deals with Chise mother's suicide and the abuse she suffered at the hands of her relatives. I also particularly like the story, because it provides inspiration for incorporating Asian characters in a Western setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}